# Feature branch creation (GitHub protected main)

## Problem

`git checkout -b feature/X origin/main` (without `--no-track`) makes the new branch **track `origin/main`**. IDE then runs:

```text
git push origin refs/heads/feature/X:main
```

Remote rejects this when `main` is protected: *You are not allowed to push code to protected branches*.

## Correct create

Default branch for this repo is **`main`**. Branch name is `feature/<KEY>`:

- Jira ticket: `feature/WISLA-<n>` (or `feature/<FULL-KEY>` if the ticket uses another prefix)
- Backlog item without Jira: `feature/FM-<n>` (key from [`BACKLOG.md`](../../BACKLOG.md))

```bash
git fetch origin main
git switch -c feature/WISLA-<n> --no-track origin/main
# or, backlog without Jira:
git switch -c feature/FM-<n> --no-track origin/main
```

Equivalent:

```bash
git checkout --no-track -b feature/WISLA-<n> origin/main
# or:
git checkout --no-track -b feature/FM-<n> origin/main
```

## Correct first push (only when user asks)

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
```

Never: `git push origin HEAD:main`, `git push -u origin HEAD:main`, or `git branch -u origin/main`.

## If a feature branch already tracks main

```bash
git branch --unset-upstream
git push -u origin HEAD
```

Or, if the remote feature branch already exists:

```bash
git branch -u origin/feature/WISLA-<n>
# or:
git branch -u origin/feature/FM-<n>
```

## Checklist after creating a branch

- `git status -sb` must **not** show `...origin/main`
- Upstream must be absent until first push, then `origin/feature/WISLA-<n>` or `origin/feature/FM-<n>`
